    reconv:['Reconversion Unit','1000 mB of hexafluoride + 500 mB of steam + 500 mB of hydrogen → 4 UO₂ dusts + 600 mB of hydrofluoric acid (provisional).','Dry route: the autoclave vaporizes the hexafluoride, the hydrolysis reactor turns it into powder with the steam and the rotary kiln reduces it with hydrogen. One grade at a time.'],
    uo2:['Enriched UO₂ dust','From the reconversion.','One item, its grade recorded; the icon changes with the grade.'],
    press:['Pellet Press','1 dust → 4 green pellets (provisional).','Rotary press: the powder is compressed into small cylinders, no additives.'],
    green:['Green pellet','From the press.','Pressed, still raw.'],
    sint:['Sintering Furnace','4 green pellets + 100 mB of hydrogen → 4 sintered pellets (provisional).','Pusher furnace: the pellets cross the tunnel in boats, in a hydrogen atmosphere, and come out dense.'],
    pel:['Sintered pellet','From the sintering furnace.','Dense and ready for the rod.'],
    tube:['Zircaloy tube','IE\'s Metal Press with the tube mold (Materials and fabrication).','The rod\'s cladding.'],
    mont:['Modular Assembly Station','Fuel jig + Fuel Assembly blueprint: 1 Zircaloy tube + 8 pellets → 1 rod (provisional).','Takes the fuel jig, the Fuel Assembly blueprint and the feeder, nondestructive inspection, welder, press and arm modules. Fills the tube and welds the end plugs, all inside the machine.'],
    rod:['Fuel rod','From the assembly.','Keeps the pellets\' grade.'],
    plate:['Zirconium plate','Common zirconium (Materials and fabrication).','The element\'s end plates and grids.'],
    mont2:['Modular Assembly Station','The same configuration: 8 rods + 2 zirconium plates → 1 element (provisional).','The same configuration (fuel jig, Fuel Assembly blueprint, the same 5 modules): the ring of 8 rods round the central rod, held between the two plates.'],
    elem:['Fuel element','From the assembly.','The cylindrical bundle the reactor takes, one per channel; its grade says how much heat it gives.'],
    reat:['Reactor','Takes the elements, one per channel in the graphite core.','See Reactor.'],
